course: dictionary
lesson: 14131
title: Small bus, big group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A minibus is a small bus. It carries about 8 to 16 passengers, which is fewer than a big bus. Look at the two parts of the word: mini means small, and bus is the bus you know.
explain: «The school minibus took our football team to the match.» The clues are school and team. A minibus carries a group of people somewhere together. Now swap your meaning into the sentence: «The school small bus took our football team to the match.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The minibus driver waved goodbye at the airport.» The driver is the person who drives the minibus. Words like this often come in phrases: by minibus, the school minibus, a minibus driver. Learn the phrase, and you will know the word.
fact: A minibus is a small bus that carries about 8 to 16 passengers.
fact: «Minibus» is made from «mini», meaning small, and «bus».
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, people often use «minibus» for school trips and sports teams.
fact: In the US, people often say «van» or «shuttle bus» instead of «minibus».
fact: In maths, you can use the number of seats in a minibus to work out how many minibuses a class needs.
exercise: «The school minibus took our football team to the match.» What is a minibus? | A bicycle with a basket | *A small bus that carries a group of people | A small boat for one person | A huge train for long journeys
exercise: «Thirty pupils are going to the museum. Each minibus carries 10 pupils.» How many minibuses are needed? | 300 | 10 | 30 | *3
exercise: «The minibus driver waved goodbye.» What is the driver's job? | To fly aeroplanes | To mend the roads | To cook dinner for the school | *To drive the minibus
test: «We travelled to the airport by minibus.» What does «by minibus» mean? | By boat | *In a small bus | On foot | On a bicycle
test: Which is the best description of a minibus? | A train with many carriages | A bus for 50 passengers | A tiny car for two people | *A small bus for about 8 to 16 passengers
exam: A class of 26 children goes on a trip, and each minibus carries 13 children. How many minibuses are needed? | 13 | 26 | *2 | 1
